Compare the two blind cleaned documents using the deterministic span ledger.
Inspect all unique spans, cite only supplied stable IDs, and let the ledger—not
raw length or boilerplate volume—determine the replacement directions.
Before returning the ledger:
1. Separate a redundant non-main wrapper from new policy propositions,
   permissions, cookie inventory, or page-specific identity.
2. Map translated facts across A### and B### before assigning either delta.
   A short extra fact/instruction still determines containment direction.
3. Check every unique span before calling it UI: a navigation teaser may be
